# Build output. The binary is built into bin/; config.Root steps out of a bin
# folder, so the app still reads storage/ and scripts/ at the repo root.
bin/
*.exe

# Everything the app accumulates: notes, saved requests, named paths and the
# environments they resolve against. All of it holds credentials, internal
# hostnames and bearer tokens, which is why it is one ignored folder rather
# than four scattered entries. storage.example/ is the template and is checked
# in.
storage/

# What Go renames the old binary to when it cannot overwrite a running exe.
# restart.sh deletes it; this is for the times you build by hand.
*.exe~

# Go
*.test
*.out

# The generated resource object (icon + DPI manifest) is checked in on purpose
# once it exists -- it is a build input, not an artifact. Do not ignore *.syso.

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
